ISO-10303-21;
/* Tsh167: TWO ADVANCED_FACEs in OPEN_SHELL — IS the empty-loop orientation mechanism; face_deg IS wired with EDGE_LOOP containing zero ORIENTED_EDGEs — IS empty loop; empty EDGE_LOOP IS wired as FACE_OUTER_BOUND of face_deg — structurally valid ref; face_good IS wired with loop_good (4 oriented edges, unit square [0,1]x[0,1]); face_deg plane IS at x=[1,2] (adjacent to face_good at x=[0,1]); FixFaceOrientation traverses outer loop to determine outward normal direction; empty loop has no traversal data — orientation assignment IS arbitrary; face_deg same_sense IS set .T. but empty loop cannot confirm/deny it; fix: validate EDGE_LOOP is non-empty before orientation traversal; emit E_FIX_FACE_ORIENT_EMPTY_LOOP when outer loop has zero edges */
